cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: Jayaputra
    given-names: Nicholas
title: >-
  moe-rl-framework: a multi-algorithm reinforcement-learning framework and a
  from-scratch Mixture-of-Experts language model family built for 6 GB GPUs
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-13
license: Apache-2.0
url: https://github.com/madharambe/moe-rl-framework
repository-code: https://github.com/madharambe/moe-rl-framework
keywords:
  - reinforcement-learning
  - mixture-of-experts
  - language-model
  - small-language-models
  - low-vram-training
  - robotics
abstract: >-
  A reinforcement-learning framework (DQN, PPO, SAC, TD3, BC, DAgger) for robotics,
  paired with a from-scratch MoE language-model family spanning roughly 50M to 587M
  parameters. Designed to train and run on a single 6 GB laptop GPU. The
  data-acquisition and corpus-curation pipeline is intentionally not part of this
  release; the framework, the model, the training code and the evaluation suites are.